 - **Fair bonus trade pricing (building-effect aware).** In `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal`, add a quick pre-check that scales a bonus’s trade value by how many **citywide building effects it actually unlocks with current techs** (granary/market/grocer/harbor/temple/monastery, etc.). Wonders/cathedrals ignored; less pronounced for coastal-building effects, as we assume to simplify many cities aren’t coastal and thus wouldn’t benefit. **Practical result (examples):** Maize/Wheat/Grapes are priced noticeably higher than Pigs/Cows; Molluscs beat low-impact foods; Iron is valued slightly less than before when it has no building bonuses (should still be valuable for units). **Effect:** shuts down early GPT farming, makes AI↔AI swaps fairer, and strengthens AI openings/midgame. See **[KI#66](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#66---fixed-and-greatly-enhanced-ai-overvaluing-bonuses-that-give-minor-effects-such-as-pig-or-cattlecow-1-health-only-etc-that-ai-would-value-the-same-as-maize-or-wheat-2-health-effectively-since-almost-all-cities-have-a-granary-and-very-early-anyways-etc-or-grapes-from-grocer-or-molluscs-from-harbor-for-example-by-adding-a-pre-check-in-cvplayeraiai_bonustradeval-to-value-relatively-more-bonuses-the-more-effects-they-provide-from-buildings-if-we-have-their-required-tech-of-these-buildings-so-that-humans-cant-abuseexploit-it-with-aggressive-trading-to-become-super-rich-xd-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc-and-also-in-ai-vs-ai-trading-each-ai-gets-best-or-more-value-out-of-the-effective-value-of-their-bonuses-at-least-more-so-now-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc)**.
 - **Bonus trade valuation uses `iAIObjective`:** In `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal`, the AI now factors each bonus’s `iAIObjective` weight directly into price—higher-priority strategic bonuses (per your weights) command more value in trades.
 - **Era- & inventory-aware relative pricing for key strategic bonuses (Horse↔Camel, Camel↔Horse, ±Elephants):** Also in `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal`, trade values now adjust by what the buyer already has and by era. Examples: Medieval buyer with **Horse/Camel** but no **Iron** values Iron ≈ x2 (to unlock Knights); by Renaissance that premium fades (Muskets don’t need any bonus; Cannons only need Iron). **Elephants** are valued in Ancient/Classical, but discounted in Medieval (≈ x0.5, for buildings at most). **Copper/Iron** are discounted in Classical if the buyer already has Camel/Horse/Elephants; Horse and Camel are treated as partial substitutes early on. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5145+) **Update:** this adjustment no longer applies to trades *within* the same master–vassal(s) locus, since it is generally in their shared interest to strengthen each other.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5135+) **Preferential master–vassal tech trading:** Heavily increase willingness to trade techs with our **master/vassal(s)**; change in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`. This synergises with the earlier “devalue techs your master/vassal already knows” change (see [Technologies (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md#technologies-ai)) and extends it **to *all* techs**, not just techs that overlap with what our master/vassal(s) already know. In one autoplay sample this led to noticeably **less overlap** and better sharing (e.g. a master gaining ~4 more and 1 fewer tech, a vassal ~2 more and 0 fewer over T250–300 compared to before). Also fixed a missing second parameter in `AI_contactRoll(CONTACT_TRADE_TECH` (according to ChatGPT 5.1), which may have contributed to earlier skew. Details: [KI#78](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#78---tremendously-improved-trade-techs-preferentially-with-our-vassals-or-master-synergises-with-the-no-overlap-previous-master-vassals-tweak--bugfix-missing-second-parameter-now-ai_contactrollcontact_trade_tech-rcontactprobmult-according-to-chatgpt-51). - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5135+) Implemented preferrential master<->vassal(s) tech trading (we are heavily more willing to tech trade with our master/vassal(s)), in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`. This synergises the previous devalue techs we can get from our master/vassal(s) change (see [Technologies (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md#technologies-ai)) and expands on it, not just techs that overlap with what our master/vassal(s) already know. In autoplay, this results for example in the master having 4 more techs and one less tech from turn 250 to turn 300 (vassal was mostly way ahead in tech) and the vassal having 2 more techs and 0 less techs, which is a massive improvement it seems, just from this change. Added a bugfix to `AI_contactRoll(CONTACT_TRADE_TECH` (was missing a second parameter according to chatgpt 5.1) which may have or not contributed to this skew in behaviour. See for details [KI#78](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#78---tremendously-improved-trade-techs-preferentially-with-our-vassals-or-master-synergises-with-the-no-overlap-previous-master-vassals-tweak--bugfix-missing-second-parameter-now-ai_contactrollcontact_trade_tech-rcontactprobmult-according-to-chatgpt-51). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5138+) **Update:** Extend the same extra trade bias to **sibling vassal↔vassal** trades. In autoplay (Ewuare with two vassals at T250), this produced broadly similar outcomes to the master–vassal–only version, which is acceptable since the change only increases trade chances (doesn’t remove any) and is therefore less likely to be harmful.
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5135+) **Preferential master–vassal tech trading:** Heavily increase willingness to trade techs with our **master/vassal(s)**; change in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`. This synergises with the earlier “devalue techs your master/vassal already knows” change (see [Technologies (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md#technologies-ai)) and extends it **to *all* techs**, not just techs that overlap with what our master/vassal(s) already know. In one autoplay sample this *seemed* to **reduce tech overlap** and **improve sharing** between vassals (who had many more techs) and their master (who now picks up more of them). Also updated `AI_contactRoll(CONTACT_TRADE_TECH` to pass an explicit probability multiplier (rather than relying on the default of 1), making tech-trade frequency more dynamic and tunable instead of solely personality-driven. See [KI#78](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#78---improved-trade-techs-preferentially-with-our-vassals-or-master-synergises-with-the-no-overlap-previous-master-vassals-tweak--add-a-second-parameter-now-ai_contactrollcontact_trade_tech-rcontactprobmult-to-have-a-more-dynamic-tech-trading-not-only-based-on-personality-according-to-chatgpt-51-and-then-corrected-by-claude-sonnet-45s-review-check-if-accurate-anyways-etc). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5138+) **Update:** Extend the same extra trade bias to **sibling vassal↔vassal** trades.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5140+) **Military-power–aware tech trade targeting:** If a potential tech-trade is *not* between members of the same master–vassal(s) locus, `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo` instead increases tech-trade contact chance toward **militarily weaker** players (safer, less likely to threaten us) and reduces it for **stronger** ones (less free value to future rivals). In one autoplay sample this seemingly produced a much closer game: the former runaway (Ewuare) was repeatedly caught up by rivals, and the game lasted to ~T419 instead of ~T288, with the lead changing hands several times. See [KI#80](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#80---tremendously-improved-ai-contacting-for-tech-trades-players-that-are-stronger-even-though-this-is-more-likely-to-be-detrimental).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5139+) **Master–vassal(s) locus first for tech trades:** Whenever the AI wants to contact other players for a tech trade in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`, it now **first checks** whether the desired tech is already tradeable inside its own master–vassal locus (master, vassals, sibling vassals). If so, it **does not ask outside civilizations for that tech**, nudging trades to stay within the group instead. In one autoplay sample this *seemed* to help Ewuare win earlier by finally picking up the Dragoon-related military tech from a vassal, while the locus kept a similar overall tech pace to previous runs. See [KI#79](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#79---improved-before-contacting-other-players-for-tech-trades-first-check-if-we-dont-already-have-the-tech-in-our-master-vassals-locus-and-if-so-dont-contact-the-other-players).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5143+) **Military priority in tech trades when behind:** When evaluating the value of a tech in trades with players outside the AI’s master–vassal(s) locus in `CvTeamAI::AI_techTradeVal`, the AI values **key military techs** (high `FLAVOR_MILITARY`) more highly if it is **weaker** than its rivals (they matter more for survival than additional economic techs); as of now most such military techs are untradeable, which is consistent with autoplay impact being small, but this may matter more if some of them become tradeable.

